@ref Decree 67/2023 Article 62(5); forks V5, V20
GIVEN `the day of the investigation result` IS A DATE
      cal                                   IS A `A calendar of working days`
GIVETH A DATE
`Article 62(5) — the last day for the police copies, the investigation result being of` `the day of the investigation result` `, on` cal MEANS
    `the working day` 5 `after` `the day of the investigation result` `on` cal

@ref Decree 67/2023 Article 62(5); fork V20
GIVETH A DEONTIC `A party under Articles 16 to 22, 62 and 75` `An act under Articles 16 to 22, 62 and 75`
`Article 62(5) — the police must provide copies of the accident documents` MEANS
    PARTY  `the traffic police or the investigating police`
    MUST   `provide copies of the police documents on the accident`
    WITHIN 5
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST   BREACH BY `the traffic police or the investigating police`
           BECAUSE "Article 62(5): copies of the police documents of Article 13(5) were not provided within 5 working days of the investigation result"

§§ `Articles 63 and 64 — the Ministries of Construction and of Transport`

-- Out of scope: Article 63 is construction insurance; Article 64 has the Ministry of Transport
-- coordinate guidance and supervision of the insurers. Neither gives a motor claimant a right.
-- src:1819 | Điều 63. Trách nhiệm của Bộ Xây dựng
-- src:1827 | Điều 64. Trách nhiệm của Bộ Giao thông vận tải

§§ `Article 65 — the Ministry of Health`

-- Read in full. The Ministry directs medical facilities to provide copies of medical records,
-- injury certificates, death notices and other papers on the emergency care and treatment of
-- road accident victims, so that insurers can complete claim files quickly. No period is given
-- and no right of the insurer or the victim against a facility is created; the documents are
-- those of Article 13(3), which row VN-10 encodes. Recorded as out of scope.
-- NOTHING in Article 65, or anywhere in the sources, is the Ministry of Health's guidance on the
-- "nồng độ cồn" (alcohol level) that Article 7(2)(đ) refers to: that guidance stays an input
-- (row VN-10) and is not in this model.
